<% content_for :title, "Open Scriptorium" %>

<%# ============================================================
  # Hero
  # ============================================================ %>
<section class="border-b border-[--color-rule]">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 py-20 sm:py-28 grid sm:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-10 gap-y-6 items-center">

    <%# Decorative illuminated initial — the same S as the navbar/favicon %>
    <div class="hidden sm:block">
      <%= inline_svg "dropcap-S", class: "dropcap-hero" %>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-[--color-ink] text-4xl sm:text-5xl leading-tight">
        An open reading room <br class="hidden sm:inline">
        for scripture and the voices that have read it.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[--color-ink-soft] font-serif leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Parallel translations of the Hebrew Bible, the Greek New Testament,
        the Septuagint, and various apocryphal texts &mdash; alongside
        historical commentary from Philo, Josephus, Origen, and later
        patristic and post-patristic voices &mdash; all
        <%= link_to "freely licensed", principles_path,
              class: "underline decoration-dotted hover:text-[--color-link]" %>,
        all cross&#8209;referenced down to the verse.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
        <%= link_to "Start reading →", works_path,
              class: "inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-[--color-ink] text-[--color-page] font-serif text-lg rounded hover:opacity-90" %>
        <%= link_to "how it works", about_architecture_path,
              class: "text-sm text-[--color-ink-soft] font-serif italic underline decoration-dotted hover:text-[--color-link]" %>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<%# ============================================================
  # Epigraph — the two opening lines as a quiet centered block
  # ============================================================ %>
<section class="border-b border-[--color-rule]">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 py-16 text-center">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[--color-ink-soft] mb-6">
      In the beginning
    </p>

    <p class="font-hebrew text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-[--color-ink] leading-loose" lang="he">
      בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים אֵת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְאֵת הָאָרֶץ׃
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[--color-ink-soft] italic font-serif">
      Genesis 1:1 (Westminster Leningrad Codex)
    </p>

    <hr class="my-8 border-[--color-rule] w-16 mx-auto">

    <p class="font-greek text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-[--color-ink] leading-loose">
      Ἐν ἀρχῇ ἦν ὁ λόγος.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[--color-ink-soft] italic font-serif">
      John 1:1 (SBL Greek New Testament)
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<%# ============================================================
  # Three-column "what's here" overview
  # ============================================================ %>
<section>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 py-16">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-[--color-ink] mb-8">In the corpus</h2>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-x-8 gap-y-10 font-serif">
      <article>
        <h3 class="text-lg text-[--color-ink] mb-2">Scripture in three languages</h3>
        <p class="text-[--color-ink-soft] leading-relaxed text-sm">
          The Berean Standard Bible in English; the Westminster Leningrad
          Codex for the Hebrew Bible; the SBL Greek New Testament; and
          Rahlfs&rsquo; Septuagint &mdash; all aligned to the same
          canonical references so they can be read in parallel.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-[--color-ink-soft] italic">
          BSB is loaded. WLC, SBLGNT, and Rahlfs are next.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3 class="text-lg text-[--color-ink] mb-2">Commentary as a first-class text</h3>
        <p class="text-[--color-ink-soft] leading-relaxed text-sm">
          Historical commentary &mdash; Philo, Josephus, Origen, the
          Ante-Nicene Fathers, and later voices &mdash; lives in the same
          schema as scripture, with cross&#8209;references that work in both
          directions.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3 class="text-lg text-[--color-ink] mb-2">Free, in the strict sense</h3>
        <p class="text-[--color-ink-soft] leading-relaxed text-sm">
          Every text in the corpus is under a license that meets the
          <a href="https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/free-sw.en.html" class="underline decoration-dotted hover:text-[--color-link]">FSF definition of free software</a>
          or the SIL Open Font License. Source code is available
          <a href="https://git.sr.ht/~sethkush/openscriptorium" class="underline decoration-dotted hover:text-[--color-link]">on sr.ht</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
